# <type>[(scope)][!]: <imperative summary, <=72 chars, no period>
#
# [optional body: what changed and why, in brief prose, wrapped at ~72]
#
# [optional footers as git trailers, e.g. Refs: ..., BREAKING CHANGE: ...]
#
# Conventional Commits 1.0.0: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
# Types: feat fix docs style refactor perf test build ci config chore revert
# Scope is optional. "!" before ":" or a BREAKING CHANGE footer marks a
# breaking change. Skip the body when the header says it all.
#
# config (anything that changes agent or tool behavior, e.g. claude/,
# settings, hooks) always needs a body with these sections, kept short:
#   Before this commit...      the behavior and the problem
#   This commit...             the change and why
#   This was tested by...      how you confirmed the new behavior
#   Impact...                  effects on behavior, performance, correctness
#   Rollback...                how to undo it, including local, unversioned files
